        {
          "t": "team",
          "kind": "biography",
          "html": "<p>Dr. Marc Ullman has been a pillar of the eye care community since 1998. Originally from Toms River, he attended Binghamton University and the Pennsylvania College of Optometry. After successfully running his own practice for nearly three decades, he transitioned ownership to Dr. Lesko and Dr. Giallombardo in early 2026 but remains a vital part of the clinical team.</p><p>Clinical Focus: Dr. Ullman is the practice’s primary resource for patients seeking relief from chronic dry eye, red eyes, and ocular injuries. He prides himself on:</p><ul><li>Being one of the first to offer new treatments to his patients.</li><li>Managing difficult contact lens fittings and chronic ocular disease.</li><li>Providing honest second opinions and surgical consultations.</li></ul><p>Dr. Ullman is known for his sensitivity to patient concerns and his commitment to the \"ultimate experience in customer service\".</p><p>Personal Interests: In his spare time, Dr. Ullman is an accomplished card magician, performing annually for the Captains Table fundraiser at the Atlantic City Boat Show. He also helps his wife, an entertainment reporter, and enjoys life with their famous furry French Bulldog, Winston.</p>",
